# ============================================================================
# FirstNest — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values:   cp .env.example .env
# `.env` is gitignored. NEVER commit real credentials to this file.
#
# Every variable below is read somewhere in the codebase. Anything prefixed
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the browser bundle and is therefore PUBLIC —
# never put a secret behind that prefix.
# ============================================================================

# ── Supabase ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project URL and anon (publishable) key. Both are public by design and are
# protected by Row Level Security on the database side.
#
# REQUIRED AT BUILD TIME: `next build` prerenders /admin/login, which constructs
# a Supabase browser client. With these unset the build fails with
# "Supabase not configured". CI may pass syntactically-valid placeholders.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# SECRET — server-only. Bypasses Row Level Security entirely.
# Used exclusively by the master-data import path (src/lib/supabase/server.ts
# → getAdminClient). Must never be exposed to the browser or to a build log.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# ── SMTP (Contact Us form: src/app/api/contact/route.ts) ────────────────────
# If SMTP_USER is empty the route logs the message instead of sending it, so
# local development works without a mail account.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
SMTP_PORT=587
# "true" only for port 465 (implicit TLS); "false" for STARTTLS on 587.
SMTP_SECURE=false
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
SMTP_FROM=no-reply@example.com

# ── Integration testing (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Point these at a DEDICATED, THROWAWAY Supabase project to enable the Row
# Level Security integration tests (tests/integration/**/*.realdb.*). Those
# tests INSERT rows — never point them at staging or production.
#
# Leave unset and the RLS suites skip themselves with a printed reason; the
# rest of the integration suite runs regardless, since it mocks the database
# driver. Apply every migration in supabase/migrations/ to the test project
# first, or the tests fail on a missing table rather than on a policy.
SUPABASE_TEST_URL=
SUPABASE_TEST_ANON_KEY=
# Optional — only for setup/teardown that must bypass RLS.
SUPABASE_TEST_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# OPTIONAL — a convenience, never a requirement.
#
# Postgres connection string for the SAME test project. When present, CI
# applies every file in supabase/migrations/ before the integration suite runs,
# so the test schema cannot drift behind the repository. The keys above cannot
# do this: they authenticate to PostgREST, which does not execute DDL.
#
# Leave it blank and nothing breaks — CI skips the migration steps and the test
# project is expected to have been migrated by hand, exactly as before. Whether
# the RLS suite runs is decided only by SUPABASE_TEST_URL and
# SUPABASE_TEST_ANON_KEY above.
#
# If you do set it, copy the SESSION POOLER string from Supabase → Settings →
# Database. Do NOT use the "direct connection" string — it resolves to IPv6
# only, and GitHub-hosted runners have no IPv6 route.
#
#   postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
#
# SECRET: a full superuser credential for the test database.
SUPABASE_TEST_DB_URL=

# ── Notes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two keys currently present in some local .env files are NOT read by any code
# and can be deleted:
#   * NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY — superseded by ..._ANON_KEY
#   * MASTER_DATA_ADMIN_TOKEN — replaced by Supabase role-based auth; see the
#     header comment in src/app/api/admin/master-data/upload/route.ts
